Parts of orchestrate/modules/M12-sensors/screen/ are a port of herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr),
commit ee5bfb5041bb3e4a49d591c72308aae3c81ecdde, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE in this
folder, copied from that commit). herdr ships no NOTICE file at this commit.

Every file below was made only from the pinned copy of that commit, never from a fresh download.

Files modified: ported from Rust and TOML to JavaScript, with changes.
  screen/claude-rules.mjs   from src/detect/manifests/claude.toml (rule set 2026.10.11.1)
  screen/match.mjs          from src/detect/manifest.rs (validator limits, the rule loop, gates and regions)
  screen/match.test.mjs     partly from src/detect/manifest/tests.rs
  screen/waiting.mjs        from src/pane/agent_detection.rs (the pending-idle confirmation)

Main changes from the original:
  - a screen no rule matches reads "unknown" (hold); herdr falls back to idle for a known agent;
  - two rules are left out: osc_progress_idle (tmux can't see the progress sequence, so the osc_progress region is
    not ported and a rule naming it is refused) and osc_title_idle (a title alone must never clear a session to idle;
    a title rule may only say working);
  - only the regions the Claude rules use are ported; the Codex prompt-marker regions and top_non_empty_lines are refused;
  - each Rust pattern is translated to an exact JavaScript equivalent (Unicode \d, \s, \w and \b, \x{...}, \z, leading
    (?i) and (?m)) or refused, never approximated;
  - a reading that is too large, or whose matching runs past a time limit, reads unknown; escape sequences are stripped
    before matching; rule ids must be unique;
  - the rules load only from the installed file: no remote download, no hot reload, no override folder;
  - the idle confirmation keeps no history between sends, never lets idle through on a time cap, counts only the
    text-region prompt rule, and also needs the hook tracker to say the session isn't waiting.
